f through a range of experiments and investigations.","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/ckfinder/userfiles/files/Forest%20School%20Curriculum%20Overview_%202.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"Forest School Curriculum Overview  2","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"The spiral nature of the Science curriculum ensures that knowledge is revisited during children\u2019s learning journey, providing students with multiple opportunities to reinforce their understanding and retention of material, allowing for deeper understanding of topics.","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/ckfinder/userfiles/files/Science%20-%20Curriculum%20Overview%20science%20new%20June.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"Science   Curriculum Overview science new June","section":"curriculum"},{"text":"Whether it be through choice of challenge, of how they record, of participation in extra-curricular clubs and opportunities, pupils are given the freedom to make choices.","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/MainFolder/documents/British-Values/British-Values.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"British Values","section":"ethos"},{"text":"In addition, children at Cherry Lane are provided with the opportunity to consolidate their skills and knowledge at art club.","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/ckfinder/userfiles/files/Art%20Curriculum%20Overview.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"Art Curriculum Overview","section":"curriculum"}],"narrativeSummary":"The school website lists music, understanding music, art club, art, emotional difficulties as music is broad. Information appears across 5 pages.","synthesisMethod":"deterministic"},{"area":"ethos","score":83,"confidence":0.885,"summary":"Strong publicly visible evidence for ethos and values (7 specific items). Listed provision includes Faiths and Beliefs, responsibility, british values, respect, ethos.","themes":["british values","community","ethos","faith","respect","safe","supportive","values"],"offerings":["Faiths and Beliefs","responsibility","british values","respect","ethos"],"signals":[{"text":"British Values: Faiths and Beliefs","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/MainFolder/documents/British-Values/British-Values.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"British Values","section":"ethos"},{"text":"Individual Liberty At Cherry Lane pupils are actively encouraged to make independent choices (particularly around learning choice and within social times), knowing that they are in a safe, secure and supportive environment \u2013 developing the children\u2019s autonomy and responsibility for their learning.","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/MainFolder/documents/British-Values/British-Values.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"British Values","section":"ethos"},{"text":"Cherry Lane Primary School \u2013 Promoting British Values Cherry Lane Primary School is committed to serving its community.","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/MainFolder/documents/British-Values/British-Values.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"British Values","section":"ethos"},{"text":"Mutual respect is embraced throughout the curriculum by providing the opportunity for students to express their views in a safe environment.","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/MainFolder/documents/British-Values/British-Values.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"British Values","section":"ethos"},{"text":"All members of the school community treat each other with respect and this is reiterated through its teaching and learning environments..","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/MainFolder/documents/British-Values/British-Values.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"British Values","section":"ethos"}],"narrativeSummary":"The school website lists Faiths and Beliefs, responsibility, british values, respect, ethos.","synthesisMethod":"deterministic"},{"area":"behaviour","score":35,"confidence":0.21,"summary":"Concrete behaviour and pastoral care details found on the school website. Listed provision includes kind, respectful.","themes":["behaviour","respectful"],"offerings":["kind","respectful"],"signals":[{"text":"Mutual Respect Our behaviour policy states that \u2018We believe good behaviour means that everyone in school is careful and kind, polite and friendly, helpful to each other, quiet and hardworking and respectful and tolerant.\u2019 Students learn that their behaviour has an effect on their own rights and those of others.","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/MainFolder/documents/British-Values/British-Values.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"British Values","section":"ethos"}],"narrativeSummary":"The school website lists kind, respectful.","synthesisMethod":"deterministic"},{"area":"send","score":35,"confidence":0.21,"summary":"Concrete SEND and inclusion details found on the school website. Listed provision includes coding, music.","themes":["sen","send"],"offerings":["coding","music"],"signals":[{"text":"Where appropriate, a multi-sensory approach to music incorporating dual coding and visuals is used to support learning for SEND pupils.","sourceUrl":"https://www.cherrylane.hillingdon.sch.uk/ckfinder/userfiles/files/Music%20Curriculum%20Overview_.pdf","sourceType":"school-document","capturedAt":"2026-09-28","pageTitle":"Music Curriculum Overview ","section":"curriculum"}],"narrativeSummary":"The school website lists coding, music.","synthesisMethod":"deterministic"},{"area":"community","score":20,"confidence":0.13,"summary":"Limited public evidence for commu